{"kind":"panel","id":"a9763a42-fa4b-4ede-8315-4c6ae6a89624","type":"59e0b89a-e487-49f8-bab8-b5bab16be14c","name":"Panel","nick":"Moment curvature","desc":"A panel for custom notes and text values","box":[0,-340,560,270],"src":[],"text":"Moment curvature - a reinforced concrete section bent until it fails.\n\nA 300 x 500 section, Concrete01 in 240 fibres, with phi 24 bars of ReinforcingSteel 30 mm in from its short faces: eight along the bottom, three along the top. 400 kN of compression is held while the curvature about y grows, in 200 increments, until the first fibre reaches its ultimate strain, bent with Direction 180 so that the eight bars are in tension.\n\nMoment Curvature Diagram draws the curve beside the section: first yield and the ultimate state marked. The panels give the moment at first yield, the ultimate moment and curvature, the curvature ductility, the cracked stiffness to first yield, and which fibre failed.\n\nTry: Axial from -400 to -1500 and watch the ductility fall; Direction 0 to bend it the other way, the three bars in tension; the bar counts at the top of the script.","colour":[0,0,0,0]}
],
